1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,221
This is ArchieOS: an operating system you talk to, built for one person and their own machines.

2
00:00:07,821 --> 00:00:16,817
Everything lives on one desktop. The orb, World, Vault, Forge, Sentry and the Stage are apps in the same window, not separate programs.

3
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:24,910
Archie can open them the way you would: it presses the dock buttons through the Stage, the one gate every action of Archie's has to pass.

4
00:00:43,321 --> 00:00:46,791
Now the request: Archie, draw the Mona Lisa.

5
00:00:47,591 --> 00:00:51,390
Archie: Sure. I'll draw the Mona Lisa for you, with my own hand on the screen.

6
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:57,892
Archie: First I'm opening Photopea, an image editor that runs in the browser, with a blank sheet the shape of the painting.

7
00:00:58,192 --> 00:01:06,020
Archie: Photopea draws its whole interface on one canvas and tells the accessibility system nothing, so I find what I need by looking at the window.

8
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:11,826
Archie: There's the paper: 429 by 640 pixels. Now I pick up the brush.

9
00:01:12,126 --> 00:01:16,006
Archie: Brush in hand, thinned to 4 pixels, with sepia ink loaded.

10
00:01:16,306 --> 00:01:27,187
Archie: I've turned the painting into 463 lines that follow her face, her hands and the landscape behind her, in two inks, sepia and red chalk, the way Leonardo drew. It should take about 2 minutes.

11
00:01:27,487 --> 00:01:38,020
Archie: Every batch of strokes goes through the Stage's gate: a permission for one operation, sealed, and checked against the window as it is right now. If you touch the mouse, control is yours and I wait.

12
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:47,964
Archie turns the painting into hundreds of pen strokes and draws them in Photopea, a real editor in a real browser, with its own pointer. We sped this part up.

13
00:01:48,264 --> 00:01:52,377
Archie: A quarter done. The darkest shapes go first, so the picture shows up early.

14
00:01:52,977 --> 00:02:04,028
Every batch of strokes is a sealed permission, checked against the window as it is right now. Move the mouse and the person has control; Archie waits, then continues the same line.

15
00:02:04,328 --> 00:02:10,124
Archie: Halfway: 241 lines so far, at about 173 pixels of line a second.

16
00:02:10,724 --> 00:02:19,406
Archie hears with NVIDIA's Nemotron speech recognition, reasons with Nemotron on Nebius, and finds what it can't name by looking at the screen.

17
00:02:19,706 --> 00:02:22,913
Archie: Now the second ink, red chalk, for the lighter tones.

18
00:02:23,706 --> 00:02:26,065
Archie: Three quarters. Now the softer tones.

19
00:02:27,706 --> 00:02:34,976
Archie: Done. 463 lines in 321 seconds, every one drawn by my own pointer, through the Stage's gate.

20
00:02:35,776 --> 00:02:40,035
ArchieOS. You say it, Archie does it, and you stay in charge.

